# data/text_files/njit_orgs.csv is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored.
#
# It is Jiti's entire knowledge base (see services/jitiCorpusService.ts), read
# from disk at boot. While it was ignored, it existed only on developer
# machines: Railway and Vercel build from this repo, so production had no
# corpus, resolveCsvPath() threw, warmUpJiti() failed, and /api/jiti never
# mounted — the chat widget silently hid itself for every student. CI failed
# the same way on a clean checkout.
#
# The file is a frozen build-time artifact (the corpus header carries a
# hardcoded "current as of" date precisely so the cached prompt prefix never
# drifts), so it belongs in version control alongside the code that reads it.
# Re-scraping it with scrape_njit_orgs.py should be a reviewable commit.
